WEBVTT

00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:05.110
Perhaps you have heard plenty about AI,

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:07.430
but you still have a simple question:

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:11.390
Where do I begin? Begin with something in
your own life.

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:13.310
Something you need to understand,

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:16.030
organize, prepare, or express.

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:20.570
Maybe you need to write a message, but you
cannot find the right words.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:25.150
Perhaps you have a project in mind and
need help organizing the steps.

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:29.370
Or you are trying to understand an
explanation that feels unnecessarily

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:30.430
complicated.

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:32.590
Those are places to begin.

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:35.770
You can speak naturally. You might say,

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:37.870
“Help me organize these ideas,”

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:40.830
or, “Explain this in plain language.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:42.890
I am unfamiliar with the subject.”

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:47.970
You do not need to know technical language
or prompt engineering to start a useful

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:52.390
conversation. Let’s say you need to write
a message asking someone to correct a

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:56.470
problem. You could tell AI what happened,
what you want corrected,

00:00:56.990 --> 00:01:00.790
and how you want the message to sound.
Then read what it gives you.

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:03.170
Does it reflect what actually happened?

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:07.210
Does it sound like you? Did it include
something you never said?

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:09.930
If something needs adjusting, say so.

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:13.110
“This sounds too formal. Make it more
natural.”

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:15.890
“You left out the most important detail.”

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:17.990
“That statement is incorrect.

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:22.610
Here is what happened.” Your participation
helps shape the result.

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:28.070
You are bringing the purpose, the facts,
and the judgment. Start with a small task

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:30.130
whose result you can comfortably check.

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:34.330
Keep private information out of the
conversation when it is unnecessary.

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:38.970
And when the answer could affect your
health, finances, or another important

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:42.010
decision, verify it with an appropriate
source.

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:44.970
You do not have to master everything
today.

00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:47.050
Choose one useful task.

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:50.050
Have the conversation. Examine the result.

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:55.670
Make a correction. That is a beginning—and
beginnings become experience through

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:59.730
practice. Thank you for joining us. We
look forward to learning with you.

